A||||2||Greg Piet||Vendors||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||04-23-2001||06:04 PM||||Someone mentioned they are sick of hearing of  bad service from vendors.<P>I agree, but some of the info needs to be addressed...  For example I was glad to hear the FOCOA was selling a "high performance" chip which was jsut a non california chip.<P>Now for all those that are weary of Fiero sellers, remember this...<P>Fiero's are not a huge aftermarket car...  these vendors could likely make oodles more cash selling other than Fiero accessories so they cannot be in the Fiero biz just to make cash.<BR>There are some vendors that I think are top notch which I have done business with such as The Fiero Store, and Tom McElroy (BTW where did he go?).  I am sure people have had problem with these vendors, and I dont really want this to turn into a "lets talk about vendors that pissed me off", but simply stating that you had a bad experience with a vendor should be adequate to "inform" the rest of us.  For example "I bought X from Y and I was not happy with the Z", or "I bought X from Y and I had a problem Z".  I think it is in poor taste to have a disagreement discussed on a public board so everyone can submit their opinions.  Resolving such issues is between the buyer and the seller.  <BR>PFF is not a judge and jury, nor should it be.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||PAUL88GT||04-24-2001||12:05 PM||||Ditto your remarks.  If you are not happy, just don't use their services or buy their products again. I see no need to make a public event out of it. I am continually amazed that a vendor can make a living out of Fiero only services and products.  Their prices have to be high just to break even.  If more go out of business, then the remaining one can raise prices because of lack of competition. It is in our best interest to keep as many Fiero vendors and service providers in business as is feasible. IMHO.<BR>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||04-24-2001||06:34 PM||||What both of you said is true, but I think a forum such as this will go along way in making vendors offer better service because they know that word of mouth is their best advertising (or worst) and this forum hits a lot of people.<P>I hate to see vendors bashed but I also hate to be taken in when I could had more info from someone else that was experienced with the company. This works no matter what your field whether it be Fieros or selling fast food hamburgers!<P>I have had dealings with very few vendors through my Fieros. Of those, some have been good, others have been terrible. I have praised the good ones (Doug at Fiero Warehouse, Rodney Dickman, Oreif) and only made very small comments about the bad ones when it was relevant (bet you thought I was gonna list them here!).<P>I guess again I am protecting free speech. Any business that is dealing with the public fairly can hold it's own in the public forum. That is the way this country was built. I agree that sometimes the name calling and stuff goes too far, but there is a need for public praise and criticism of businesses in our society.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 04-24-2001).]||||reg||1
